(footprint "RP2350_Zero_Header_23p"
  (version 20221018)
  (generator "handwritten")
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "RP2350-Zero pin-socket footprint (female, board side), 23 physical pins (20 GPIO + 5V/GND/3V3). Origin = module center. LAYOUT CORRECTED 2026-08-21/22 (three rounds): (1) user physically counted the real module's pins and found right column = 9 (not 8) and bottom row = 5 (not 6), left column stays 9; (2) user pointed out RP2350-Zero is explicitly sold as fitting a standard 2.54mm perfboard grid, so all 23 holes must sit on ONE uniform 2.54mm grid -- discarded earlier non-grid sub-pixel offset readings in favor of pure grid math, making the right column Y-symmetric with the left column; (3) user then caught that the bottom row was still placed one extra grid step below the left/right columns' last row (Y=-12.70mm), which does not match the module's real physical extent -- corrected to Y=-10.16mm, the SAME row as the left/right columns' last pin, so the bottom row simply fills the gap between the two columns' bottom ends at one shared Y. Final layout, all coordinates exact 2.54mm-grid multiples, forming a 'U'/staple shape (2 columns of 9 + 1 connecting row of 5, all 7 X-positions from -7.62 to +7.62 in the bottom row actually line up on one continuous 2.54mm-pitch row when you include the two column-end pins): Left column (9 pins, X=-7.62mm): Y=+10.16,+7.62,+5.08,+2.54,0,-2.54,-5.08,-7.62,-10.16 = 5V,GND,3V3,GP29,GP28,GP27,GP26,GP15,GP14 (top to bottom). Right column (9 pins, X=+7.62mm): SAME Y values as left column (Y-symmetric) = GP0,GP1,GP2,GP3,GP4,GP5,GP6,GP7,GP8 (top to bottom). Bottom row (5 pins, Y=-10.16mm -- SAME row as the last left/right pins, centered on X=0): X=-5.08,-2.54,0,+2.54,+5.08 = GP13,GP12,GP11,GP10,GP9 (left to right); GP12/GP13 = USB host D+/D-, adjacent by construction. Pin IDENTITIES (which physical pin carries which GPIO name, e.g. left-to-right order in each row) are still not individually re-confirmed against the Waveshare wiki pinout image -- only the pin COUNT and GRID POSITIONING are now high-confidence. Visually compare against the wiki pinout image before gerber ordering.")
  (tags "RP2350-Zero header socket 23pin")
  (attr through_hole)
  (fp_text reference "REF**" (at 0 -14) (layer "F.SilkS")
    (effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
  )
  (fp_text value "RP2350_Zero_Header_23p" (at 0 14) (layer "F.Fab")
    (effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
  )
  (fp_text user "pin IDENTITY not re-confirmed vs wiki image (count+grid are confirmed)" (at 0 -10.9) (layer "Cmts.User")
    (effects (font (size 0.8 0.8) (thickness 0.12)))
  )
  (pad "1" thru_hole circle (at -7.62 10.16) (size 1.6 1.6) (drill 1.0) (layers "*.Cu" "*.Mask"))
